{
 "name": "Coracle",
 "note": "The 12-cell Coracle for the film's 1:1 view (1.2 cells per Exhibit B grain), built by coracle.py's s12() as a reduction of the 24 and a step up from b10. Rest is 12 x 10 inside a 12 x 12 grid; row 0 is left free for the lift, row 11 for the frames whose bead hangs lower. The keel is clay shade, umber only at each row's ends. The line is tied at column 7, a column right of the keel's right-middle column, so the line is 1.5 cells and the 2x2 bead 2 cells right of the bowl's axis (between columns 5 and 6): never on it. In every frame a row of clay lies between the eyes and the lit lip. idle12: rest, lift (the bowl rises a pixel, rigid; the bead held, so a second pixel of line shows), settle (one row shallower, the lower hull two pixels fuller, the clay row under the eyes kept; keel and bead where they were). blink12: its own frame, every 4-6 bobs, never in the idle; the lids shut and the bead lights a second cell. lean12: travelling right, travelling left (runs of 4, the eyes ahead, the bead trailing on a kinked line; both drawn, not mirrored, so the light stays upper left). glance12: left, right. inspect12: toward a thing on the left, then the right: not lifted, leaning toward it, the eyes on it and narrowed to their lower row (looking down at it), the bead hanging straight from its tie. discover12: the eyes widen a row, downward; a one-pixel hop with the bead brightening; settles with the bead swung out a cell. construct12: lets the bead down on a kinked line, the eyes narrowed on it and toward it; the touch (3 px kinked, the bead 3 cells off the axis, brightening; the work sits just under the frame). rest12: at anchor (the bead on the ground just under the frame, the line kinked, eyes half closed, glints kept); rocks (the bowl down a pixel, the line slack).",
